{"id": "EUVD-2026-102555", "enisaUuid": "933fedf4-c021-31a8-b81a-c11236e57d4b", "description": "FreeRDP from 3.30.0 before 3.32.0 contains a resource exhaustion vulnerability in the rdpecam client that lets malicious RDP servers request unadvertised camera media types. Attackers can send a StartStreamsRequest with oversized dimensions to force large pending-sample allocations and reconfigure the local camera through the HAL.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T01:17:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:05:37", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-xq87-9rrm-6wqw", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-from-3.30.0-before-3.32.0-resource-exhaustion-via-rdpecam-startstreamsrequest"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111374", "GHSA-p6rp-88mp-xhw3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f240b63c-429a-3f22-aeaa-4c205b38f460", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.30.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3c12b4bb-d4e2-3990-870e-9cc3864da309", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}